  "description": "",
  "lore": "Knitted by Nanny Pottlewick for a child who never came home from the dunes. She stitched its mouth shut the night it began to hum.\n\nIt is always found at the foot of a bed, never the same bed twice. Those who wake beside it say their left foot has gone cold, and that it stays cold for the rest of their lives.\n\nDo not ask what it is wearing the sock over. It will tell you.",
